{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1092", "sample_idx": 24, "model_name": "mistralai/ministral-14b-instruct-2512", "content": "**A Whirlwind Adventure in Japan**\n\nJapan was a dream come true—where neon-lit streets meet ancient temples, and every bite feels like a work of art. Our trip began in **Tokyo**, where the hum of the Shinkansen bullet train whisked us from the bustling streets of Shinjuku to the serene hills of **Kyoto** in under three hours.\n\nIn Kyoto, we wandered through **Fushimi Inari**, the famous shrine with thousands of vermilion torii gates winding up the mountain. The crisp air and golden light filtering through the gates made it feel like stepping into a painting. At night, **Gion’s** lantern-lit alleys came alive with geisha spotting tours and traditional teahouses serving matcha with delicate precision.\n\nNext, we ventured to **Osaka**, where the towering **Dotonbori** district dazzled with giant crab signs and sizzling takoyaki stalls. The food was unforgettable—melty okonomiyaki, crispy ramen, and, of course, wagashi (Japanese sweets) that tasted like clouds.\n\nOur final stop was **Hiroshima**, a place of history and healing. The **Peace Memorial Park** was solemn and moving, but the resilient spirit of the city shone through in its rebuilt streets and the iconic **Miyajima Island**, where the floating torii gate at **Itsukushima Shrine** glowed against the sunset.\n\nJapan left us breathless—modern and traditional, chaotic and calm, all in perfect balance. Already counting the days until we return.", "logprobs": [{"token": "**", "logprob": -0.06550939381122589}, {"token": "A", "logprob": -0.30262133479118347}, {"token": " Wh", "logprob": -0.04418794438242912}, {"token": "irl", "logprob": -0.012623289600014687}, {"token": "wind", "logprob": -5.936446541454643e-05}, {"token": " Adventure", "logprob": -1.174424409866333}, {"token": " in", "logprob": -0.07322251796722412}, {"token": " Japan", "logprob": -0.005896553862839937}, {"token": "**